  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Crlp/282/2022 on 27 January, 2022 Author: Cheekati Manavendranath Roy Bench: Cheekati Manavendranath Roy The Hon'Ble Sri Justice Cheekati Manavendranath Roy Criminal Petition Nos.281, 282, 285, 291, 292 & 294 of 2022 Common Order:",
    "facts": "These criminal petitions are filed under Section 482 Cr.P.C. seeking to quash the FIRs in Crime No.7 of 2022 of Chinna Bazar Police Station, SPSR Nellore District, registered for the offences under Sections 272 and 273 of IPC and Sections 22, 23 r/w 5(1) of COTPA Act; Crime No.6 of 2022 of Chinna Bazar Police Station, SPSR Nellore District, registered for the offences under Sections 272 and 273 of IPC and Sections 22, 23 r/w 5(1) of COTPA Act; CC No.284 of 2018 on the file of learned Additional Judicial Magistrate of First Class, Kovvur, SPSR Nellore District, filed for the offences under Sections 353 and 273 of IPC and Section 59(i) of Food Safety and Standard Act; Crime No.405 of 2021 of Tadikonda Police Station, Guntur District, registered for the offences under Sections 273 and 420 of IPC and Sections 57(1), 58, 59 and 63 of Food Safety and Standard Act; Crime No.445 of 2021 of Dachepalli Police Station, Guntur District, registered for the offences under Sections 420 and 273 of IPC and Section 7(1) r/w 20(1) of COTPA Act; and Crime No.7 of 2022 of Thotapalli, Gudur Police Station, SPSR Nellore District, registered for the offences under Sections 272 and 273 of IPC and Sections 22, 23 r/w 5(1) of COTPA Act.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners would submit that these are all covered matters in view of the earlier orders passed by this Court in Crl.P. Nos.5421 of 2019 and batch and Crl.P. Nos.2966 of 2021 and batch, whereby this Court has [LEAKAGE_MASK] several FIRs registered for the similar offences based on identical facts. Therefore, the petitioners are similarly placed and they are also entitled for quash of the FIRs registered and charge sheet filed against the petitioners.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners would submit that these are all covered matters in view of the earlier orders passed by this Court in Crl.P. Nos.5421 of 2019 and batch and Crl.P. Nos.2966 of 2021 and batch, whereby this Court has [LEAKAGE_MASK] several FIRs registered for the similar offences based on identical facts. Therefore, the petitioners are similarly placed and they are also entitled for quash of the FIRs registered and charge sheet filed against the petitioners.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
